# Storybook embeds (iframe architecture)

The site embeds Storybook stories via `ComponentPreview` (`src/LayoutComponents/ComponentPreview.jsx`).
Current tag: `<object>` — migrating to `<iframe>` in the next update.

## Must follow

### 1. Lazy loading (non-negotiable)

Every embed **must** use `loading="lazy"`:

```html
<iframe src="..." loading="lazy" />
```

This is the single biggest performance win — defers network, CPU, and memory until the embed scrolls near the viewport. All modern browsers support it natively.

### 2. Defer rendering — don't mount on page load

Never render an embed eagerly on page load. Mount the `<iframe>` only when the user **needs** it:

- **Tab click** — embed loads when user switches to the tab containing it
- **Section expand** — embed loads when an accordion/collapsible opens
- **Scroll into view** — use `IntersectionObserver` as a gate before mounting
- **Explicit interaction** — "Load preview" button for heavy pages

The `ComponentPreview` should accept a `lazy` prop (default `true`) that wraps the iframe in an `IntersectionObserver` gate. When `lazy` is true, render a lightweight placeholder (title + footer + skeleton) until the card enters the viewport, then mount the iframe.

### 3. Reuse a single iframe when possible (preferred architecture)

On pages with **3+ previews** (e.g. Toolbar with Preview, Variants, Sizes), prefer:

- One visible `<iframe>` that switches `src` based on selection
- A sidebar list, tab bar, or segmented control to pick the active story
- Changing `src` on an existing iframe is faster than mounting/unmounting multiple iframes

Use multiple iframes only when previews must be visible simultaneously (e.g. side-by-side comparison). For sequential viewing (tabs, accordions), always reuse one iframe.

### 4. Security — minimal sandbox

Use the **least permissions needed**:

```html
<iframe
  src="..."
  sandbox="allow-scripts"
  referrerPolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
/>
```

- `allow-scripts` — required for Storybook to render components
- Do **not** add `allow-same-origin` unless the story specifically needs it (breaks sandbox isolation)
- Do **not** add `allow-popups`, `allow-forms`, `allow-downloads` unless explicitly required
- Always set `referrerPolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"`

### 5. Fixed heights — no auto-resize libraries

Do **not** use `iframe-resizer` or similar libraries. They cause layout thrashing and continuous `postMessage` traffic.

Instead:
- Use a fixed `height` prop (default 300px)
- Offer a small set of preset heights per story type if needed (compact: 200, default: 300, tall: 450)
- Resize only on explicit user action (e.g. a drag handle), never automatically

### 6. Virtualize on catalog/list pages

If a page renders **10+ preview cards** (e.g. a components catalog with inline previews):
- Use `react-window` or TanStack Virtual to only mount visible cards
- Combine with `loading="lazy"` on each iframe
- Unmounted cards should not have iframes in the DOM at all

## iframe tag template

When migrating `ComponentPreview` from `<object>` to `<iframe>`:

```jsx
<iframe
  src={activeUrl}
  title={title}
  width="100%"
  height={height}
  loading="lazy"
  sandbox="allow-scripts"
  referrerPolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
  style={{ display: 'block', border: 'none' }}
/>
```

## Storybook URL patterns

| Purpose | URL format |
|---------|------------|
| Story canvas only | `https://o9arvo-storybook.vercel.app/iframe.html?id={story-id}&viewMode=story` |
| Light theme | Append `&globals=theme%3Ao9theme` |
| Dark theme | Append `&globals=theme%3Ao9dark` |
| Docs page | Replace `viewMode=story` with `viewMode=docs` and use `--docs` suffix on story id |

The `/iframe.html` path is Storybook's built-in canvas endpoint — it is not an iframe itself; it is a standalone HTML page suitable for embedding.

## ComponentPreview props reference

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `title` | string | — | Footer title |
| `description` | string | — | Footer subtitle |
| `storybookUrl` | string | — | Light-theme story URL |
| `storybookDarkUrl` | string | — | Dark-theme URL (enables sun/moon toggle) |
| `height` | number | 300 | Embed height in px |
| `children` | ReactNode | — | Fallback content when no URL provided |

## When editing ComponentPreview

- Preserve dark-mode styling (uses `useTheme()` like GrayBgCard/WhiteBgCard)
- Keep the sun/moon theme toggle functional
- Keep the "Open in new tab" link
- Update this rule if props or architecture changes
